.Dd March 8, 2025
.Dt SCHED 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm sched_get_thread ,
.Nm sched_yield ,
.Nm sched_set_affinity
.Nd kernel scheduler and thread management
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/sched.h
.Ft thread_t *
.Fn sched_get_thread "int tid"
.Ft void
.Fn sched_yield "void"
.Ft int
.Fn sched_set_affinity "int tid" "uint32_t mask"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm sched
subsystem manages process threads and CPU scheduling in the Substrate kernel.
.Pp
.Fn sched_get_thread
retrieves the thread structure associated with the given
.Fa tid .
This operation is performed in O(1) time using an index-encoded TID scheme,
where the TID contains both the slot index and a generation counter.
.Pp
.Fn sched_yield
voluntarily relinquishes the CPU, allowing the scheduler to select the next
best thread to run based on priority and scheduling class.
.Pp
.Fn sched_set_affinity
sets the CPU affinity mask for the specified thread.
The
.Fa mask
is a bitmask where each bit represents a valid CPU ID.
Attempts to set an affinity mask with no valid CPUs will fail.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn sched_get_thread
returns a pointer to the
.Vt thread_t
structure if found, or
.Dv NULL
if the TID is invalid or the thread does not exist.
.Pp
.Fn sched_set_affinity
returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure (e.g., invalid TID or mask).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kthread 9 ,
.Xr proc_find 9
